HEAD:.beads/issues.jsonl:7:{"id":"bdc-3ku","title":"ANC-005: sc-cron stays a general job scheduler","description":"sc-cron, the SQLite cron job scheduler crate, must remain a general-purpose job scheduler that the sc-runtime repository can copy.","notes":"Quote (verbatim, immutable): I expect 'sc-cron' to be a general tool that can be used for scheduling jobs. [...] should retain that general purpose shape for porting (copying) to sc-runtime.\nAnchor record: docs/plans/phase-b/anchors/anchors.json. The description is the testable statement; change it only through jev_judge.py update --statement.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"decision","created_at":"2026-10-25T20:17:08.263803Z","created_by":"randlee","updated_at":"2026-10-25T20:17:08.322082Z","source_repo":"beads-cache","source_repo_path":"/Users/randlee/github/beads-cache","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["anchor","anchor:ANC-005"]}
HEAD:.beads/issues.jsonl:16:{"id":"bdc-7of","title":"ANC-007: Stop hook returns continue, disable or delete","description":"sc-cron, the SQLite cron job scheduler crate, must let a schedule define a stop hook that returns the string value continue, disable or delete.","notes":"Quote (verbatim, immutable): sc-cron should include the ability to define a `stop hook` [...] allow stop hook to return a stringenum with values 'disable', 'delete', 'continue' (or similar)\nAnchor record: docs/plans/phase-b/anchors/anchors.json. The description is the testable statement; change it only through jev_judge.py update --statement.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"decision","created_at":"2026-10-25T20:17:08.898049Z","created_by":"randlee","updated_at":"2026-10-25T20:17:08.960525Z","source_repo":"beads-cache","source_repo_path":"/Users/randlee/github/beads-cache","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["anchor","anchor:ANC-007"]}
HEAD:.beads/issues.jsonl:35:{"id":"bdc-g4s.1","title":"ANC-002 plan questions","description":"```json\n{\n  \"questions\": {\n    \"addressed\": {\n      \"criteria\": {\n        \"no\": \"The item does not say the bd sync runs from a SQLite cron table: it is silent about when the sync runs, says only that a schedule is needed or will be decided later, names a different source of times, or is not about the bd sync.\",\n        \"unclear\": \"The item mentions a cron table or a schedule near the bd sync, but it cannot be told whether the bd sync's times come from a SQLite cron table.\",\n        \"yes\": \"The item says the bd sync runs at the times set by a row or entry in a SQLite cron table kept by beads-cache, such as sc-cron's table in the cache file.\"\n      },\n      \"instructions\": \"`anchor.statement` requires one specific thing: the bd sync runs at the times set in a SQLite cron table that beads-cache keeps. Does `item.text` say this: that the bd sync's schedule is a row or entry in a SQLite cron table (for example sc-cron's cron table, job table or schedule table in the cache file) and that the sync runs at the times that row sets? Judge only whether this specific content is present. Do not judge whether anything in the item conflicts with it.\",\n      \"type\": \"choice\"\n    },\n    \"contradicted\": {\n      \"criteria\": {\n        \"no\": \"Nothing in the item rules out running the bd sync at the times set in a SQLite cron table, whether or not the item mentions it.\",\n        \"unclear\": \"The item describes how the bd sync is triggered, but it cannot be told whether that excludes the SQLite cron table.\",\n        \"yes\": \"The item plans a schedule, trigger or design for the bd sync that cannot be reconciled with running it at the times set in a SQLite cron table.\"\n      },\n      \"instructions\": \"`anchor.statement` requires beads-cache to run its bd sync at the times set in a SQLite cron table. Does `item.text` plan something that rules this out? Conflicts include: the sync runs only when an external scheduler (OS cron, systemd, launchd, Task Scheduler, CI) invokes a command; the sync's times come from somewhere other than a SQLite cron table, such as a fixed timer or an interval in a config file; the cache keeps no schedule of its own. These are not conflicts: silence about scheduling; a command that runs one extra sync on demand while the schedule stays in the cron table; letting a consumer disable the built-in sync row or run its own sync method instead. Judge conflict only.\",\n      \"type\": \"choice\"\n    },\n    \"relevant\": {\n      \"criteria\": {\n        \"no\": \"The item's work does not involve the bd sync: it is about another part of the system, such as packaging, release channels, documentation, or a scheduled job other than the bd sync.\",\n        \"unclear\": \"The item mentions syncing or scheduling, but it is not possible to tell whether the bd sync is meant.\",\n        \"yes\": \"The item schedules, runs, triggers, configures or changes the bd sync (the tick), for example its schedule row, its scopes or filters, its hooks, or a command that runs it.\"\n      },\n      \"instructions\": \"The state holds one planning item (`item.title`, `item.text`) and one anchor (`anchor.statement`, `anchor.scope`) about the bd sync: beads-cache's job that syncs issues from bd, the beads issue-tracker CLI, into the cache. The bd sync is also called the tick, as in `bdc cache tick` or `bd_cache_sync::tick`. Does the work in `item.text` schedule, run, trigger, configure or change the bd sync? Judge only whether the item's work involves the bd sync. Do not judge whether the item obeys `anchor.statement`.\",\n      \"type\": \"choice\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n","notes":"Sealed question set digest: af6112f31a0bba4416ac7fe678cc5bb1a149a583cc2d8f1ad40e3c4195bfd692\nTuning history (plan-anchor/tuning-history/2) sha256: fe2415e98257a340906578cb4e7a6af5f5cbac5c2b7e853488cdc0cd2a43c946\n```json\n{\"e