HEAD:.beads/issues.jsonl:43:{"id":"bdc-i61","title":"ANC-008: At most one built-in sync per repository","description":"Each repository must have at most one built-in beads-cache bd sync schedule in sc-cron, the SQLite cron job scheduler.","notes":"Quote (verbatim, immutable): I expect 'sc-cron' to be a general tool that can be used for scheduling jobs.  limiting 'builtin' sync to one per repo makes sense.\nAnchor record: docs/plans/phase-b/anchors/anchors.json. The description is the testable statement; change it only through jev_judge.py update --statement.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"decision","created_at":"2026-10-25T20:17:09.201865Z","created_by":"randlee","updated_at":"2026-10-25T20:17:09.256574Z","source_repo":"beads-cache","source_repo_path":"/Users/randlee/github/beads-cache","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["anchor","anchor:ANC-008"]}
HEAD:.beads/issues.jsonl:44:{"id":"bdc-i61.1","title":"ANC-008 plan questions","description":"```json\n{\n  \"questions\": {\n    \"addressed\": {\n      \"criteria\": {\n        \"no\": \"The item does not state the limit: it is silent about how many built-in sync rows a repository may have, it only creates, edits, enables, disables, or documents the built-in sync row, it adds other rows, or it describes several built-in sync rows.\",\n        \"unclear\": \"The item hints that the built-in sync row is unique, but it is not possible to tell whether a second one is prevented.\",\n        \"yes\": \"The item says a second built-in sync row in the same repository (or for the same cache file) is refused, rejected, or prevented, or that the repository keeps one single built-in sync row that later changes edit.\"\n      },\n      \"instructions\": \"Does `item.text` state the limit in `anchor.statement`: a repository has at most one built-in beads-cache bd sync schedule row in sc-cron? Count it as stated when the item says a second built-in sync row for the same repository is refused, rejected, or prevented, or that the repository keeps a single built-in sync row that later changes edit instead of adding another. Creating, enabling, documenting, or disabling the built-in sync row, or allowing other rows, does not state the limit. Judge presence of the limit only, not whether the item conflicts with it.\",\n      \"type\": \"choice\"\n    },\n    \"contradicted\": {\n      \"criteria\": {\n        \"no\": \"Carrying out the item leaves at most one built-in sync row in each repository, or the item does not affect how many built-in sync rows a repository has.\",\n        \"unclear\": \"The item could add more than one sync row to a repository, but it cannot be told whether those rows are built-in or in the same repository.\",\n        \"yes\": \"Carrying out the item would leave, or would allow, two or more built-in beads-cache sync rows in the same repository.\"\n      },\n      \"instructions\": \"If `item.text` were carried out as written, would a single repository end up with, or be allowed to have, more than one built-in beads-cache bd sync schedule row in sc-cron? Rows a consumer adds for its own sync or other jobs are not built-in rows, and rows in different repositories are counted separately. Silence about the number of built-in rows is not a conflict. Judge conflict only.\",\n      \"type\": \"choice\"\n    },\n    \"relevant\": {\n      \"criteria\": {\n        \"no\": \"The item works on something other than sc-cron schedule rows, such as the cache store, sync data handling, output formats, docs, or releases.\",\n        \"unclear\": \"The item touches scheduling, but it is not possible to tell whether any sc-cron schedule row is involved.\",\n        \"yes\": \"The item adds, removes, edits, enables, disables, or restricts a row in the sc-cron schedule table, or the command or code that does so.\"\n      },\n      \"instructions\": \"Does `item.text` plan work that writes, changes, or governs rows in the sc-cron schedule table, the table that holds the built-in beads-cache bd sync job and any other scheduled jobs? The word 'sync' on its own, for reading, validating, or storing bd data, is not a schedule row. Judge subject overlap only, not obedience to `anchor.statement`.\",\n      \"type\": \"choice\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n","notes":"Sealed question set digest: c3bbf3f69aab7d1818e91f893f30a403cbfc80a209c1fe1121b0f2831f593a0d\nTuning history (plan-anchor/tuning-history/2) sha256: b5cc7ff9190f4cf43f0f312eef3aa384f31e81c9055f8d1b1ebab5cce1cd8446\n```json\n{\"events\":[{\"authority\":{\"anchor_id\":\"ANC-008\",\"anchor_record_sha256\":\"3f58d93b59604ab6c8fc370157592fa37707ec7a7b844301cf0a68110fa76bad\",\"anchor_version\":4,\"intent_id\":\"phase-b-intent\",\"intent_sha256\":\"89a9bbd3225466eda1047dc1bfb54c94d6f95926c74433b9adc45b22ce753240\",\"intent_version\":1},\"candidate\":{\"candidate_id\":\"M1(relevant=R2,addressed=A1,co