te five-second ownership. Do not widen timeouts, add retries, waive this run or call a later green run a fix.\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Exact b7de8e9879503353879c500edacf12a6832d709d run41776396362 Windows job126397662727, raw rust-qa-hosted-c2-windows.log:1950-1965: first read-only negative records kill/reap5.005945s and original500ms observation; next busy-persistence child output contains only running1test and test name; assertion1084 fails worker operation did not run; store33passed1failed, exit101. Source schedule.rs:1056-1095 starts an owned child, finishes at5s, checks timeout/cleanup receipt/under7s, then checks post-call marker and500ms-expiry output. Busy path:861-919 includes database preparation, worker call, stall marker and timed completion observation. Shared store tree6286e1f33ae881d92e7acaf95852c4010ab82cbc, source blobd30f281677d56389285827faabeb4d8aace48758 and helper blobd312b5608d5bd50511647227cf865938219e3efb match C1/C2/adbc exactly.\",\n        \"limits\": \"Timing classification describes the observed watchdog/receipt failure only. Logs do not locate the child at timeout or prove host scheduling, SQLite malfunction, missing product cancellation, orphaning, or a newly introduced source regression. Missing receipt does not prove the operation never began or returned. This is separate from the earlier Windows CTRL_BREAK issue, startup shutdown correction, and the repaired FTQ009 unbounded fixture lifetime.\",\n        \"correlation\": \"Same actual occurrence as independent rust-qa-agent RQA9-001; retain this ID, not a duplicate FTQ ID.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"total_findings\": 1,\n      \"critical\": 0,\n      \"important\": 1,\n      \"minor\": 0,\n      \"sprint_verdict\": \"FAIL; real shared-store Windows failure and unchanged SDK/logging/graph/CI blockers remain\"\n    },\n    \"dispositions\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"FTQ-011\",\n        \"status\": \"fixed_close_supported_for_exact_C1\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Owning independent source/evidence assessment supports closure at a753d279. process_ids_using passes caller absolute deadline to owned inventory; no independent50ms cap or minimum50ms slice remains. Parsing/output/identity consume that same deadline. Initial100ms drain, absolute250ms quiescence and1s cleanup,5s fixture lifetime remain. Incomplete scans cannot satisfy stable quiescence; two complete stable stopped censuses, actual root wait and fresh final whole-session empty census are required before cleaned=true. One cleanup attempt is enforced, including Drop handoff. Recovery obtains fresh evidence; it does not convert original failed/timeout fixture status into success. Independent Rust first-run18/18 includes real116.818417ms delayed inventory, original failed child preserved, stopped inventory timeout/unwind and persistent-incomplete cleanup retaining false receipt. Four unchanged source-free negatives remain failed101 with empty ownership audits before driver fallback. Original14/15 and13/15 failures retained.\",\n        \"scope_limit\": \"C2 still contains old session_fixture.rs blob8eed049 baseline; imported C2 FTQ011 is not closed by C1 correction until consumed and qualified there.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"FTQ-009\",\n        \"status\": \"closed_preserved_for_original_unbounded_lifetime\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Exactly filtered owned child bounds all three store fixture paths; timeout/unwind actually kill and wait root. Current independent Darwin store5/5 demonstrates post-call stall/500ms timeout for all3. Actual Windows RQA9-001 does not demonstrate return to the old unbounded ownership mechanism; retain it separately and require investigation.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"FTQ-010\",\n        \"status\": \"closed_preserved_for_original_orphan_and_inventory_stall\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Session established before production Python launch; child-written registry is diagnostic. Root/session/descendant and inventory