isolated boundary gate FAILURE; C2 Windows shared store33/1 failure additionally preserved. No whole required CI green claim.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"ARCH-001\",\n        \"status\": \"open\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Published public canonical-event receiver composition gap remains; direct bd-cache-sync->sc-command at Cargo.toml31 and cron_log.rs3 unchanged. Strict approved introducer boundary unchanged; helper correction supplies no SDK seam.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RBQA-F001\",\n        \"status\": \"open\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Distinct canonical carried boundary ID retained. Direct sync->sc-command receiver dependency remains outside published sc-cron-only exception; no approved boundary amendment or actual edge removal.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"QA2-001\",\n        \"status\": \"open\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Actual exact-head hosted boundary job126399209278 independently fetched by Rust fails isolated Python graph on direct sync->sc-command; API graph and checker4 pass. This is not flaky failure suppression; keep existing guard failing until authorized remediation.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"RQA9-001\",\n        \"status\": \"open\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Independent owning assessment accepts actual Windows occurrence and source correlation as Important failed shared-fixture qualification. Underlying cause unknown; required investigation stated in finding.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"review_evidence\": [\n      \"Adopted cursor-orchestration and flaky-test-qa role. Full rendered JSON read; exact assigned C1 branch/head and paired C2 head verified clean before review. Current targeted source examined independently, not inferred from parent claims.\",\n      \"Independently computed all review-target blob identities against prior adbcc88d review. Only helper/test call sites, triage and sprint narrative changed;159 production Rust files unchanged. Absent crates/sc-cron files are already migrated to published dependency and were absent at baseline too. Prior unchanged-scope review retained through byte comparison; fresh helper/startup/shared-store occurrence review performed.\",\n      \"No new Cargo/build/test/binary execution by this reviewer; optional sole Cargo grant was not needed. Read independent Rust compilation/command/raw execution receipts and the actual developer delayed/hung tests and50ms-mutant failure. No repeated18/full1171/platform matrix or repeat-until-green.\",\n      \"Intentional80ms delay is injected while an owned shell has acknowledged kernel STOP, then CONT allows exec of real ps. It exercises delay beyond former50ms while retaining existing250ms budget; it is not readiness inferred from sleep. Hung inventory uses acknowledged self-stop, timeoutkill/wait and unwind ownership. Persistent incomplete census test verifies3actual reaped children, false receipt, no fresh second-cleanup budget and no Drop retry.\",\n      \"Quiescence resets previous census after inventory error, never treats incomplete output as empty, includes observing-process validity check and rechecks identity before signals. Final drain includes the root after real wait. Preliminary inventory error recovery is accepted only after fresh complete quiescence/rootjoin/final emptiness under original absolute deadlines. Original fixture outcome stays failed in both source and raw negative output.\",\n      \"Following cm rule b-mr7cp6x0-ipdnhs: platform observations are kept distinct. Current C1 core three-platform SUCCESS and local lints/tests do not imply overall requiredCI or C2Windows success.\",\n      \"Actual hosted Windows failure path is src/schedule.rs1084, not tests/schedule_store.rs. Store source/helper unchanged across paired heads; no precise child state, phase, scheduler delay or SQLite cause can be recovered from existing child output. A Darwin repeat would not establish the Windows cause.\",\n      \"Prior C2FTQ006 retraction remains scoped to healthy-kernel sameUID process ownership. No unsupported credential changes or mathematical SIGKILL/wait progress guarantee used as new finding.\"\n    ],\n    \"retained_failures\": [\n      {\n        \"original\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-8/flaky-retained-lifecycle-failure.log\",\n        \"durable\": \"/Users/randlee/github/beads-cache-worktrees/sprint/c-1-runtime-migration/.cursor/qa-evidence/phase-c/c-1/qa-8/logs/flaky-retained-lifecycle-failure.log\",\n        \"sha256\": \"1e202e2df51a1a49bbde10aaa993d2ff070a047976c1a9513c0b7ed11344d6de\",\n        \"durable_sha256\": \"1e202e2df51a1a49bbde10aaa993d2ff070a047976c1a9513c0b7ed11344d6de\",\n        \"identical\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"original\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-8/rust-qa-lifecycle.log\",\n        \"durable\": \"/Users/randlee/github/beads-cache-worktrees/sprint/c-1-runtime-migration/.cursor/qa-evidence/phase-c/c-1/qa-8/logs/rust-qa-lifecycle.log\",\n        \"sha256\": \"4bc8dfacfbb074f8f0bfd406341331dbd2d2923f6cdd90892977d4953ce4dc40\",\n        \"durable_sha256\": \"4bc8dfacfbb074f8f0bfd406341331dbd2d2923f6cdd90892977d4953ce4dc40\",\n        \"identical\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"artifacts\": {\n      \"rust-qa-lifecycle.log\": {\n        \"path\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-9/rust-qa-lifecycle.log\",\n        \"sha256\": \"43e1668f5dd6b1b3f4cb13caf52b3c947cba59d282fad0f8b21071f57ac0718a\"\n      },\n      \"rust-qa-store.log\": {\n        \"path\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-9/rust-qa-store.log\",\n        \"sha256\": \"24ed83ec0fd5b7d7ed1a657f5954c6a2718d2afd4878c43b29df50b50f77ff93\"\n      },\n      \"rust-qa-c2-rebuilt-probe.log\": {\n        \"path\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-9/rust-qa-c2-rebuilt-probe.log\",\n        \"sha256\": \"f985ffea867b12e038c4e6c85b18506dc0f6401605835be4003aacf09097610d\"\n      },\n      \"rust-qa-c2-service.log\": {\n        \"path\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-9/rust-qa-c2-service.log\",\n        \"sha256\": \"04009f1ca33c8