HEAD:.cursor/qa-evidence/phase-c/c-2/qa-5/validated-phase-protocol-delivery/validated-phase-protocol-before.json:20:      "text": "@prefix triage: <urn:beads-cache:triage:> .\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:id \"RSH-001\" ; triage:sprint \"c-2\" ; triage:severity \"BLOCKING\" ; triage:location \"crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs:115\" ; triage:source \"qa-3 owning reviewer fenced JSON\" ; triage:status \"open\" ; triage:record \"{\\\"adr\\\": \\\"ADR-BDC-0016\\\", \\\"correlated_owner_ids\\\": [\\\"RSH-001\\\"], \\\"description\\\": \\\"C2 Application::shutdown at lib.rs:110-118 still stops admission/StopFlag and joins its cron task and real readiness worker. The cron task calls cron_run at :82, whose cron_run_hurried at cron.rs:198-224 awaits WorkerHandle::shutdown before ordinary expiry kill. Published sc-cron0.1.1 scheduler.rs:912-954 still waits task.await after deadline expiry, while worker.rs:539-550 awaits uncancelled blocking store work. sc-runtime0.1.1 builder.rs:342-344 correctly retains instance ownership until application cleanup returns. Therefore contended store work can extend the daemon cleanup/instance-lock interval beyond the approved finite bound. C1 RSH-001 remains OPEN at this concrete C2 occurrence; the independent readiness/test corrections do not change that public production shutdown API.\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"crates/bd-cache-service/src/lib.rs\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"RSH-001\\\", \\\"line\\\": 115, \\\"owning_sprint\\\": \\\"c-1\\\", \\\"remediation\\\": \\\"Keep C2 blocked on the existing C1/upstream bounded worker/store shutdown fix and qualify it through the actual daemon cleanup/instance-lock path after an authorized baseline is available. Preserve real owned joins and child reap before unlock; do not infer closure from happy-path tests, detach work through timeout/drop, relax the lifecycle bound or implement a local scheduler fork.\\\", \\\"reviewer\\\": \\\"arch-qa\\\", \\\"rule\\\": \\\"RULE-ADR-CODE\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"BLOCKING\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"OPEN\\\", \\\"verification\\\": \\\"QA3: exact native crates tree, manifests/lock and governing architecture objects are byte-identical to QA2; concrete C2 occurrence directly rechecked, original owner ID retained.\\\"}\" .\n\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:latestReview \"C2QA4 at3282502831d33350622f56a9ddc8f5d24a4efc8a, PR109comment6608719324: remains open; no waiver.\" .\n\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:producerConsumption \"{\\\"c2_disposition\\\": \\\"implemented_pending_C2_QA\\\", \\\"consumer_scope\\\": \\\"C2 retains actual cron worker/readiness joins and requires independent QA5 caller binding; producer qualification does not close this occurrence\\\", \\\"owning_c2_status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"producer_report\\\": \\\"https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6621585641\\\", \\\"producer_scope\\\": \\\"RSH-001 production bounded shutdown and FTQ-009/FTQ-010 complete fixture cleanup independently qualified; whole C1 FAIL with 3 Blocking and 1 Important, PR108 not merged\\\", \\\"producer_source\\\": \\\"5255610a16ef4500f0af508e29a533707a4a3e0a\\\", \\\"qualification\\\": \\\".cursor/qa-evidence/phase-c/c-1/qa-7/component-qualification.json\\\"}\" .\n\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:qualifiedShutdownConsumption \"{\\\"implementation_state\\\": \\\"implemented_pending_C2_QA\\\", \\\"independent_C2_QA\\\": \\\"pending parent QA5\\\", \\\"integration\\\": \\\"d4af63d2a81bebd6b5b967ef5032731152bb5f7c\\\", \\\"receipt\\\": \\\"docs/plans/phase-c/evidence/c-2-qualified-shutdown-consumption.md\\\", \\\"source_commit\\\": \\\"5255610a16ef4500f0af508e29a533707a4a3e0a\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Producer RSH-001 independently qualified in C1 QA7, exact source consumed unchanged. Owning C2 RSH-001 remains open pending independent QA5 of actual application binding and retained cleanup joins.\\\"}\" .\n\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:startupReopenEvidence \"{\\\"finding\\\": {\\\"category\\\": \\\"correctness\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Independent source-free public-API probe at45c9dd1 retains Composed::schedule_store(), starts its ordinary set_enabled write under a real external BEGIN IMMEDIATE writer and proves actual same-connection mutex contention via a bounded worker view notification. Then Application::start(grace250ms) and actual shutdown remain pending902.343541ms (>original2T500ms); after explicit writer ROLLBACK, management returnsOk(true), both probe/management threads join and Application returnsOk at978.142166ms. Direct probe process exited0 and was waited/reaped; no product edits/private access. Source cron171 warn_at_startup()->schedule.rows760 reads original management store before stop loop and deadlines200+.\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"RSH-001\\\", \\\"issue\\\": \\\"The qualified post-start worker/store correction is consumed correctly, but the public startup path still reads warnings through the unbounded management view before observing stop. A supported retained schedule view can hold that shared connection during an ordinary management write, extending an actual Application shutdown beyond2T before the bounded worker starts.\\\", \\\"line\\\": 171, \\\"owning_sprint\\\": \\\"c-1\\\", \\\"probe_receipt\\\": \\\"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-2/qa-5/startup-probe-result.json\\\", \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Route this newly discovered startup occurrence to the C1 shared cron producer owner: make startup work stop-aware and cooperatively bounded within the existing absolute2T lifetime, preserving real owned joins and ordinary independent management policy. Add a deterministic early-stop/shared-connection regression. No new SDK surface, detached task, timeout widening or management-policy suppression is required by this finding. After the producer correction, consume the exact source and requalify the caller.\\\", \\\"reviewer\\\": \\\"rust-qa-agent\\\", \\\"scope_limit\\\": \\\"This is the generic public cron/start-stop contract and a real public Application API reproduction. Current stock daemon composition itself does not launch this independent pre-start same-connection management writer; no stock-daemon HTTP reproduction is asserted. Genuine post-start worker/store/reader caller qualification remains credited.\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"critical\\\"}, \\\"owner_task\\\": \\\"/root/c2_rustqa4\\\", \\\"probe\\\": \\\"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-2/qa-5/startup-probe-result.json\\\", \\\"qualified_shared_producer\\\": \\\"5255610a16ef4500f0af508e29a533707a4a3e0a\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"New supported public Application/SystemSchedules startup occurrence owned by C1 cron prelude, no documented startup exclusion; stock daemon HTTP reproduction not claimed. Prior post-start fixes remain credited.\\\", \\\"source_commit\\\": \\\"45c9dd13258482ba8af3e5cfeae5ce146b120453\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\"}\" .\n\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:startupCandidateProducerHistory \"{\\\"context\\\": \\\"Immutable C1 candidate history retained on merge; owning C2 status and earlier history above stay authoritative. C1 QA8 remains FAIL; no acceptance inferred.\\\", \\\"producer_ttl\\\": \\\"@prefix triage: <urn:beads-cache:triage:> .\\\\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:id \\\\\\\"RSH-001\\\\\\\" ; triage:sprint \\\\\\\"c-1\\\\\\\" ; triage:severity \\\\\\\"critical\\\\\\\" ; triage:location \\\\\\\"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs:198\\\\\\\" ; triage:source \\\\\\\"qa-3 owning reviewer fenced JSON\\\\\\\" ; triage:status \\\\\\\"open\\\\\\\" ; triage:record \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"carry_forward_from\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"qa-2 specialist output; unchanged production source, still open\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OPEN at assigned HEAD: crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs:198 still constructs worker.shutdown(now + shutdown_timeout), :202 awaits it, :21