ocess stall, not a mathematical demand to bound kernel syscalls.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"line\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 143, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"mechanism\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"unbounded_wait\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"recommendation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Give each inventory invocation an owned bounded lifetime with stdout/stderr handling, timeout kill/reap and unwind cleanup, or replace it with an inventory interface that cannot block the supervising thread indefinitely. Count inventory time in the original250ms/750ms cleanup budgets; preserve real PythonJob, strict inner bounds and the repaired pre-registration/session ownership. Add a stalled-inventory negative that fails finitely and cleans both inventory and fixture process trees.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"important\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Python lifecycle SessionFixture cleanup, including rejected_second_start_cannot_reset_the_first_workers_shutdown_deadline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"inherited_kernel_kill_wait\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"not_reopened\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"original_registration_orphan\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fixed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-6/flaky-inventory-stall-probe.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"QA6 /root/c1_flaky5 finalfencedJSON exactdc468b9c\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"open\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\" .\\\\n\\\\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-010> triage:qa6Correction \\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"bounded owned inventory; Linux raw SID validation; real Python lifecycle and existing strict budgets retained\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"FTQ-010\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"implementation_state\\\\