HEAD:docs/architecture.md:151:| `sc-cron` (prototype, moves to sc-runtime) | SQLite-backed cron scheduler extracted from an earlier in-house scheduler: expression parse, next-run computation, jitter, missed-tick replay, stop check before every run, generation fencing of overlapping runs, schedule store with a rusqlite implementation. Generic job payload and error type; no caller types (ADR-BDC-0006). Sprint b-8 (ADR-CRON-0009): a hook target per row (`TargetResolver`, `Scheduler::spawn_worker_with`, REQ-CRON-0016), `Scheduler::run_due_with`, the exported child-process supervisor `sc_cron::process` (`ChildSpec`, `ChildEnv`, `TempCwd`, `supervise`; `PythonHook::with_env`; `HookOutput::stop_decision` / `run_outcome`, REQ-CRON-0018); `StopDecision::Stop` removed | cron, chrono, tokio (with process, io-util), rusqlite (bundled), async-trait, serde_json, getrandom, process-wrap (hook process group and job object), tempfile (a child's working directory), tracing | a; b (b-6, b-7, b-8) |
HEAD:docs/bd-cache-sync/architecture.md:17:| `payload` | `BUILTIN_ROW`, `PYTHON_ROW`, `SyncRow` (the two names as sc-cron's, built once), `SyncPayload` (one constructor, `decode`, which reads the value in place; `to_json` cannot fail: every path is checked to be UTF-8 when the value is built), `BuiltinPayload` (`Default`), `PythonPayload` (private fields, a `RunTimeout`), `PostSyncHook`, `EnvNames` (the child environment allowlist), `TrustedInterpreter` (absolute regular executable, UTF-8, then `PythonHook::new`; the 5 s import check), `Field` (the refusals' field names) |
HEAD:docs/bd-cache-sync/architecture.md:24:| `job` | `BuiltinSyncJob`, `sync_resolver` (the per-row `TargetResolver`; it mints each launch's run id and checks trust on the opened cache file), `SyncContext`, `SyncFiles`, `join_idle` |
